msgstr "Returns a default move when no analysis is available."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch._get_fallback_move:5 of
msgid "Premier coup possible ou None"
msgstr "First move possible or None"

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch._hash_state:1 of
msgid ""
"Génère un hash unique pour un état de jeu. Utilisé pour la table de "
"transposition et la détection de cycles."
msgstr ""
"Generates a unique hash for a game state. Used for transposition table and "
"cycle detection."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch._hash_state:5 of
msgid "État à hasher"
msgstr "State to hash"

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch._hash_state:6 of
msgid "Hash de l'état"
msgstr "State Hash"

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch.get_statistics:1 of
msgid "Retourne des statistiques sur la recherche effectuée."
msgstr "Returns statistics on the search performed."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.pnsearch.PNSearch.get_statistics:3 of
msgid "Dictionnaire de statistiques"
msgstr "Statistics dictionary"

#: ../../classes/pnsearch.rst:15
msgid ""
":class:`PNSearch` implémente l'algorithme **Proof-Number Search (PN-"
"Search)**, conçu pour prouver ou réfuter mathématiquement une position de "
"jeu. Contrairement aux algorithmes heuristiques, PN-Search garantit une "
"réponse exacte (PROVEN / DISPROVEN) dans la limite de noeuds allouée."
msgstr ""
":class:`PNSearch` implements the **Proof-Number Search (PN-Search)** "
"algorithm, designed to mathematically prove or disprove a game position. "
"Unlike heuristic algorithms, PN-Search guarantees an exact answer (PROVEN / "
"DISPROVEN) within the allocated node limit."

#: ../../classes/pnsearch.rst:21
msgid ""
"Allis, L. V. (1994). *Searching for Solutions in Games and Artificial "
"Intelligence.*"
msgstr ""
"Allis, L.V. (1994). *Searching for Solutions in Games and Artificial "
"Intelligence.*"

#: ../../classes/pnsearch.rst:26
