#: ../../classes/state.rst:4
msgid "State — Représentation d'un état de jeu"
msgstr "State — Representation of a game state"

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state:2 of
msgid "Module state"
msgstr "Module state"

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state:4 of
msgid ""
"Ce module définit la classe abstraite :class:`State`, base de toutes les "
"représentations d'état de jeu dans PyAdverseSearch."
msgstr ""
"This module defines the abstract class :class:`State`, the basis of all game"
" state representations in PyAdverseSearch."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:1 of
msgid "Classe abstraite représentant un état de jeu."
msgstr "Abstract class representing a game state."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:3 of
msgid ""
"Chaque jeu doit fournir sa propre sous-classe de :class:`State` en "
"implémentant au minimum la méthode :meth:`_apply_action`. Les autres "
"méthodes délèguent leurs appels à l'instance de :class:`Game` associée via "
"l'attribut ``game``."
msgstr ""
"Each game must provide its own subclass of :class:`State` by implementing at"
" least the :meth:`_apply_action` method. Other methods delegate their calls "
"to the associated :class:`Game` instance via the ``game`` attribute."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:8 of
msgid ""
"Représentation du plateau de jeu (liste de listes, tableau NumPy, etc.)."
msgstr "Representation of the game board (list of lists, NumPy array, etc.)."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:10 of
msgid ""
"État précédent dans l'arbre de recherche (``None`` pour l'état racine)."
msgstr "Previous state in the search tree (``None`` for root state)."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:13 of
msgid ""
"Référence à l'instance :class:`Game` pour accéder aux fonctions de règles."
msgstr ""
"Reference to the :class:`Game` instance to access the rules functions."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State:17 of
msgid ""
"L'attribut ``game`` doit être initialisé avant tout appel aux méthodes "
"``_possible_actions``, ``_is_terminal``, ``_utility`` ou ``_evaluate``."
msgstr ""
"The ``game`` attribute must be initialized before any call to the "
"``_possible_actions``, ``_is_terminal``, ``_utility`` or ``_evaluate`` "
"methods."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State._possible_actions:1 of
msgid "Retourne la liste des actions légales depuis cet état."
msgstr "Returns the list of legal actions from this state."

#: PyAdverseSearch.classes.state.State._possible_actions:3 of
